flag is True, and result is SELECT FRPM.CDSCode, MAX(FRPM.Percent (%) Eligible FRPM (K-12))
FROM frpm AS FRPM
JOIN schools AS SCHOOL ON FRPM.cds = SCHOOL.CDSCode
WHERE SCHOOL.County = 'Alameda' AND SCHOOL.District = 'K-12'
GROUP BY FRPM.CDSCode;

This SQL query will select the CDSCode and the highest eligible free rate for K-12 students in the schools in Alameda County from the frpm table by joining it with the schools table on the CDSCode column. The query will only return the results for schools in Alameda County and for schools that are K-12 schools, by filtering on the County and District fields. The query will group the results by CDSCode and will return the maximum value of the 'Percent (%) Eligible FRPM (K-12)' field for each CDSCode. This will give the highest eligible free rate for K-12 students in the schools in Alameda County.
