flag is True, and result is SELECT c.Phone
FROM schools c
JOIN satscores s ON c.CDSCode = s.cds
WHERE s.rtype = 'sat12'
AND s.AvgScrRead / s.NumTstTakr > 15
ORDER BY s.AvgScrRead / s.NumTstTakr DESC
LIMIT 3;

This query will select the phone numbers of the schools that have a SAT excellence rate of at least 15, which is achieved when the average score on the reading section of the SAT is at least 15 times the number of students who took the test. The query will join the schools and satscores tables on the CDSCode field and will only select schools where the rtype in satscores is 'sat12' (the reading section of the SAT). The WHERE clause filters the results to only include schools with a SAT excellence rate of at least 15, and the ORDER BY clause sorts the results in descending order by SAT excellence rate. The LIMIT clause is used to only return the top 3 schools with the highest SAT excellence rate.
