Here is an example of the SQL query to achieve this:
```
SELECT schools.DistrictCode
FROM schools
INNER JOIN frpm
ON schools.CDSCode = frpm.CDSCode
WHERE frpm.Magnet = 0 AND schools.City = 'Fresno'
```
This query will return the `District Code` for all schools that offer a magnet program and are located in the city of Fresno, as well as the district code for the school that does not offer a magnet program in the city of Fresno.

If you only want to return the district code for the school that does not offer a magnet program in the city of Fresno, you can add an additional condition to the WHERE clause to filter the results to only include schools that do not offer a magnet program. Here is an example of how to do this:
```
SELECT schools.DistrictCode
FROM schools
INNER JOIN frpm
ON schools.CDS
