flag is True, and result is To find the alternative languages available for card named Annul numbered 29, we need to join the "cards" table with the "set\_translations" table and filter by the card name and number. Then we can join the "translations" table to get the alternative language codes. Here's the SQL statement to achieve this:
```vbnet
SELECT c.name AS card_name, st.language AS language, t.language_code
FROM cards c
JOIN set_translations st ON c.id = st.setCode
JOIN set_translations t ON st.id = t.id AND t.language_code <> st.language_code
WHERE c.name = 'Annul' AND st.id = 29;
```
This query will return the name of the card, the language of the primary translation, and the language code of the alternative translation(s) for card named Annul numbered 29. If there are no alternative translations, the language code column will be
