flag is True, and result is Assuming that the "cards" table has a foreign key "duelDeck" that references the "sets" table, and that the "sets" table has a column named "duelDeck" which contains the name of the duel deck, we can use the following SQL query to get the cards that belong to duel deck 'a':
```vbnet
SELECT cards.id, cards.name
FROM cards
JOIN sets ON cards.duelDeck = sets.duelDeck
WHERE sets.duelDeck = 'a'
```
This query will join the "cards" and "sets" tables on the "duelDeck" column, and then filter the results to only include cards that belong to duel deck 'a'. The "id" and "name" columns of the "cards" table will be selected in the results.

To get the ID of the cards that belong to duel deck 'a', we can modify the above query to select the "id" column instead of the "name" column:
```vbnet
SELECT cards.id
FROM cards
JOIN sets ON cards.duelDeck = sets.duelDeck
WHERE sets.duelDeck = 'a'
```
This query will return a list of card IDs that belong to duel deck 'a'.
