flag is True, and result is To find the cards that are only available in paper and Japanese language, you would need to join the "cards" table with the "set\_translations" table and the "legalities" table. You would also need to filter the results by card availability and language.

Here is an example of the SQL query that would achieve this:
```
SELECT c.id, c.name, c.text
FROM cards c
JOIN set_translations st ON c.id = st.setCode
JOIN legalities l ON c.id = l.uuid
WHERE st.language = 'Japanese' AND l.status = 'available in paper'
```
This query would select the card id, name, and text from the "cards" table, and join it with the "set\_translations" and "legalities" table on the card id. It would then filter the results by language and availability.

It is important to note that this is just an example and the final SQL query would depend on the specific requirements of the application.
