To get the names of cards with an original type of Creature - Elf and the date of rulings for these cards, you can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT name, ruling_date
FROM sets
JOIN rulings ON sets.uuid = rulings.uuid
WHERE original_type = 'Creature - Elf'
```
This query will join the sets and rulings tables on the uuid column, and will only return rows where the original\_type is 'Creature - Elf'. It will then return the name and ruling\_date columns from the sets and rulings tables.

You can also filter the ruling\_date by adding where clause like
```
SELECT name, ruling_date
FROM sets
JOIN rulings ON sets.
