   TEXT,\n    text                    TEXT,\n    toughness               TEXT,\n    type                    TEXT,\n    types                   TEXT,\n    uuid                    TEXT              not null\n        unique,\n    variations              TEXT,\n    watermark               TEXT\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "foreign_data"\n(\n    id           INTEGER not null\n        primary key autoincrement,\n    flavorText   TEXT,\n    language     TEXT,\n    multiverseid INTEGER,\n    name         TEXT,\n    text         TEXT,\n    type         TEXT,\n    uuid         TEXT\n        references cards (uuid)\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "legalities"\n(\n    id     INTEGER not null\n        primary key autoincrement,\n    format TEXT,\n    status TEXT,\n    uuid   TEXT\n        references cards (uuid)\n            on update cascade on delete cascade\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "rulings"\n(\n    id   INTEGER not null\n        primary key autoincrement,\n    date DATE,\n    text,\n    uuid TEXT\n        references cards (uuid)\n            on update cascade on delete cascade\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE rulings_dg_tmp\n(\n    id   INTEGER not null\n        primary key autoincrement,\n    date DATE,\n    text TEXT,\n    uuid TEXT\n        references cards (uuid)\n            on update cascade on delete cascade\n)\n\n-- External Knowledge: Spanish refer to language; Percentage refer to DIVIDE(SUM(ID where language = \'Spanish\'), COUNT(id))*100\n-- Using valid SQLite and understading External Knowledge, answer the following questions for the tables provided above.\n-- Calculate the percentage of cards in Spanish. List them by name.\nGenerate the SQL after thinking step by step: \nSELECT '}]}
flag is True, and result is To calculate the percentage of cards in Spanish, you can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT
    name,
    (SUM(CASE WHEN language = 'Spanish' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(id)) * 100 AS `Percentage in Spanish`
FROM
    cards
WHERE
    language = 'Spanish'
ORDER BY
    `Percentage in Spanish` DESC;
```
This query calculates the percentage of cards in Spanish by dividing the sum of the values of the `cards` table where the `language` column is equal to `'Spanish'` by the count of the `id` column. The result is multiplied by 100 to convert it to a percentage and is then displayed as the `Percentage in Spanish` column in the output. The query also filters the results to only include cards where the `language` column is equal to `'Spanish'`. The results are sorted by `Percentage in Spanish` in descending order.

The output of this query
