flag is True, and result is To find the release date of the set of cards with the name 'Ancestor's Chosen', you can use the following query:
```
SELECT releaseDate FROM sets WHERE name = 'Ancestor's Chosen';
```
This will retrieve the release date of the set with the name 'Ancestor's Chosen' from the sets table.

Note that the query assumes that the name of the set is spelled correctly and is exactly 'Ancestor's Chosen'. If the name is misspelled or has extra characters, the query will not match any rows in the sets table and will return an empty result.

You can also use the following query to get all sets that have the name 'Ancestor's Chosen':
```
SELECT * FROM sets WHERE name = 'Ancestor's Chosen';
```
This will retrieve all rows from the sets table where the name column matches the exact string 'Ancestor's Chosen'.
