flag is True, and result is To answer the question "Among the users who have more than 100 upvotes, how many of them have more then 1 downvotes?", we need to first identify the users who have more than 100 upvotes and then count the number of users who also have more than 1 downvotes.

Here is the SQL query to achieve this:
```vbnet
SELECT COUNT(*) AS num_users
FROM users
JOIN (
  SELECT user_id
  FROM votes
  WHERE vote_type_id = 1 AND upvotes > 100
) upvoted_users
ON users.id = upvoted_users.user_id
JOIN (
  SELECT user_id
  FROM votes
  WHERE vote_type_id = 1 AND downvotes > 1
) downvoted_users
ON users.id = downvoted_users.user_id;
```
This query uses a subquery to identify the users who have more than 100 upvotes and another subquery to identify the users who have more than 1 downvotes. The two subqueries are joined together using the user\_id column from both tables. Finally, the COUNT() function is used to count the number of users who have both more than 100 upvotes and more than 1 downvotes.

The result of this query will be the number of users who meet both of these criteria.
