flag is True, and result is p.PostId, COUNT(pc.Id)
FROM Posts p
JOIN PostHistory ph ON p.Id = ph.PostId
JOIN PostComments pc ON ph.PostId = pc.PostId
JOIN Users u ON p.OwnerUserId = u.Id
WHERE u.Age > 65
GROUP BY p.PostId
HAVING COUNT(pc.Id) > 19;

This query will find all posts that are owned by a user who is 65 years old or older, and have a score of over 19. It joins the Posts, PostHistory, and PostComments tables to get the necessary information, and filters the results by the user's age and the score of the posts. The query then groups the results by post ID and counts the number of comments for each post. Finally, it filters the results to only include posts that have more than 19 comments.
