First, we will join the tables postHistory and posts on the CreationDate and PostId columns, respectively:
```vbnet
SELECT ph.PostId, p.Body, th.ExcerptPostId
FROM postHistory th
JOIN posts p ON th.PostId = p.PostId
JOIN postHistory ph ON th.RevisionGuid = ph.RevisionGuid
WHERE th.PostTypeId = 1 -- 1 is the type ID for regular posts
AND th.CreationDate >= '2022-01-01' -- change this to the desired date range
AND th.Name NOT LIKE 'd%e%t%a%r%' -- exclude revisions
AND th.Name NOT LIKE 'c%a%t%e%r%' -- exclude conflicting revisions
AND th.Name NOT LIKE 'b%i%l%l%e%r%' -- exclude invalid revisions
AND p.ExcerptPostId IS NOT NULL -- exclude posts without excerpts
AND th.ExcerptPostId IS NULL -- exclude posts with excerpts
AND ph.UserId = 21 -- change this to the desired user ID
ORDER BY th.CreationDate DESC
```
This query will give us the most recent post with type ID 1 (regular post) within the specified date range that matches the "bayesian" tag in the postHistory table.

Next, we will join the postHistory table with the tags table on the TagName column:
```sql
SELECT p.PostId, p.Body, t.TagName
FROM postHistory th
JOIN posts p ON th.PostId = p.PostId
