```
SELECT PostId, Body
FROM Posts
WHERE Tags.Count = (SELECT MAX(Tags.Count) FROM Tags)
```
This will select the `PostId` and `Body` columns from the `Posts` table, and filter the results to only include posts where the number of tags is equal to the maximum number of tags across all posts.

To get the body of the post, you can modify the query like this:
```
SELECT Posts.PostId, Posts.Body
FROM Posts
INNER JOIN Tags ON Posts.Id = Tags.ExcerptPostId
WHERE Tags.Count = (SELECT MAX(Tags.Count) FROM Tags)
```
This will join the `Posts` table with the `Tags` table on the `ExcerptPostId` column, and filter the results to only include posts where the number of tags is equal to the maximum number of tags across all posts.
