ocation        TEXT null,\n    AboutMe         TEXT     null,\n    Views           INTEGER          null,\n    UpVotes         INTEGER          null,\n    DownVotes       INTEGER          null,\n    AccountId       INTEGER          null,\n    Age             INTEGER          null,\n    ProfileImageUrl TEXT null\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE votes\n(\n    Id           INTEGER  not null\n        primary key,\n    PostId       INTEGER  null,\n    VoteTypeId   INTEGER  null,\n    CreationDate DATE null,\n    UserId       INTEGER  null,\n    BountyAmount INTEGER  null,\n        foreign key (PostId) references posts (Id)\n            on update cascade on delete cascade,\n        foreign key (UserId) references users (Id)\n            on update cascade on delete cascade\n)\n\n-- External Knowledge: highest score comment refers to Max(comments.Score)\n-- Using valid SQLite and understading External Knowledge, answer the following questions for the tables provided above.\n-- What is the title for the post which got the highest score comment?\nGenerate the SQL after thinking step by step: \nSELECT '}]}
flag is True, and result is To get the title of the post that got the highest score comment, you can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT posts.Title
FROM posts
JOIN comments ON posts.Id = comments.PostId
JOIN postHistory ON comments.Id = postHistory.CommentId
JOIN postLinks ON postHistory.PostId = postLinks.RelatedPostId
WHERE postHistory.RevisionGUID IS NOT NULL
AND postHistory.RevisionGUID = (SELECT MAX(postHistory.RevisionGUID) FROM postHistory WHERE postHistory.PostId = posts.Id)
AND postHistory.Score = (SELECT MAX(comments.Score) FROM comments WHERE comments.PostId = posts.Id)
AND postHistory.UserId = (SELECT Id FROM users WHERE users.DisplayName = 'highest_score_comment_user' LIMIT 1)
```
This query joins the `posts`, `comments`, `postHistory`, and `postLinks` tables to get the post with the highest score comment and its title. The `WHERE` clause filters the results to only include posts with a non-null `RevisionGUID` (i.e., the latest revision) and with the highest score comment. The subquery in the `WHERE` clause gets the `RevisionGUID` with the maximum `RevisionId` for the corresponding `PostId`. The subquery in the `SELECT` clause gets the `Id` of the user who made the highest score comment.
