-- Give the total number of posts with more than 50 comments.
Generate the SQL after thinking step by step:
SELECT COUNT(Id)
FROM posts
JOIN comments ON posts.Id = comments.PostId
WHERE comments.Score > 50;

Explanation:
This query will join the posts and comments tables on the Id column. It will then filter the results to only include posts where the score of the comment is greater than 50. The COUNT() function will count the number of such posts, and the result will be returned.
