flag is True, and result is To get all posts that are related to post ID 61217, you can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT PostId, CreationDate, Score, Title, Tags, CommentCount, UserId
FROM posts
WHERE RelatedPostId = 61217;
```
This query will select the PostId, CreationDate, Score, Title, Tags, CommentCount, and UserId columns from the posts table, and filter the results to only include posts that have a RelatedPostId of 61217.

To get the popularity of the post, you can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT ViewCount
FROM posts
WHERE RelatedPostId = 61217;
```
This query will select the ViewCount column from the posts table, and filter the results to only include posts that have a RelatedPostId of 61217. The ViewCount column represents the number of views that a post has received.

Alternatively, you can use a single query to get both the posts and their related post's viewcount by joining the posts table with itself.
```
SELECT p1.*, p2.ViewCount
FROM posts p1
JOIN posts p2 ON p1.RelatedPostId = p2.Id
WHERE p1.RelatedPostId = 61217;
```
This query will join the posts table with itself, based on the RelatedPostId and Id columns, and filter the results to only include posts that have a RelatedPostId of 61217. It will also select the ViewCount column from the posts table as a column of the joined table, so you will be able to see the viewcount of the related post.

