1. First, we need to find the post ID 395 in the posts table:
```sql
SELECT Id, PostId, Score, CreationDate, Title, Body
FROM posts
WHERE Id = 395;
```
2. Then, we can retrieve the link type ID associated with the post by joining the postHistory table on the post ID:
```sql
SELECT ph.PostHistoryTypeId, ph.RevisionGUID, ph.CreationDate, ph.Text
FROM postHistory ph
JOIN posts p ON p.Id = ph.PostId
WHERE p.Id = 395;
```
3. Finally, we can retrieve the link type ID by joining the postLinks table on the link type ID:
```sql
SELECT pl.RelatedPostId, pl.LinkTypeId
FROM postLinks pl
JOIN postHistory ph ON pl.PostHistoryTypeId = ph.PostHistoryTypeId
WHERE ph.PostId = 395;
```
The final SQL query would look like this:
```vbnet
SELECT ph.PostHistoryTypeId, ph.RevisionGUID, ph.CreationDate, ph.Text
FROM postHistory ph
JOIN posts p ON p.Id = ph.PostId
JOIN postLinks pl ON pl.PostHistoryTypeId = ph.PostHistoryTypeId
WHERE p.Id = 395;
```
This query retrieves the link type ID and the associated link details for post ID 395.
