flag is True, and result is To get all post IDs with a score greater than 60, and the user IDs that created these posts, you can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT PostId, UserId
FROM posts
WHERE Score > 60
```
This will return a list of post IDs and the user IDs that created those posts, where the score is greater than 60.

To sort the results by post score in descending order, you can use the following query:
```
SELECT PostId, UserId
FROM posts
WHERE Score > 60
ORDER BY Score DESC
```
This will return the same list of post IDs and user IDs, but the results will be sorted by post score in descending order, so the posts with the highest scores will be at the top of the list.

To further filter the results to only include posts that have a score of exactly 60, you can use the following query:
```
SELECT PostId, UserId
FROM posts
WHERE Score = 60
```
This will return a list of post IDs and user IDs for posts that have a score of exactly 60.

To get the same information for all posts, regardless of score, you can use the following query:
```
SELECT PostId, UserId
FROM posts
```
This will return a list of all post IDs and user IDs for all posts in the database.
