flag is True, and result is To determine the names of badges that users who have the highest reputation obtained, we can use the following SQL query:

SELECT b.Name
FROM badges b
JOIN users u ON b.UserId = u.Id
WHERE u.Reputation = (SELECT MAX(Reputation) FROM users);

This query joins the badges table with the users table on the UserId foreign key. It then filters the results to only include badges that were earned by users who have the highest reputation. This is accomplished by using a subquery to find the maximum reputation score in the users table and then using that value to filter the results in the main query. The final result is the name of the badges that the users with the highest reputation obtained.
