```
SELECT comment
FROM comments
WHERE postId = <postId>
  AND creationDate = '2010-07-19 19:37:33'
```
Replace `<postId>` with the actual ID of the post for which you want to retrieve the comment. This query will select the `comment` field from the `comments` table, and return only the rows where the `postId` matches the specified post ID and the `creationDate` matches the specified date.

If you want to retrieve all comments for the post, regardless of the `creationDate`, you can use the following query:
```
SELECT comment
FROM comments
WHERE postId = <postId>
```
Again, replace `<postId>` with the actual ID of the post for which you want to retrieve the comments. This query will select all rows from the `comments` table where the `postId` matches the specified post ID.
