flag is True, and result is To list the names of users who have obtained the Organizer badges, we can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT Users.DisplayName
FROM Users
JOIN Badges ON Users.Id = Badges.UserId
JOIN BadgesTypes ON Badges.TypeId = BadgesTypes.Id
WHERE BadgesTypes.Name = 'Organizer';
```
This query will join the Users table with the Badges table on the UserId column, and will join the BadgesTypes table on the TypeId column. It will then filter the results to only include rows where the Name of the BadgesTypes table is 'Organizer'. Finally, it will select the DisplayName column from the Users table.

This query will return a list of all users that have obtained the Organizer badges, along with their display names.
