flag is True, and result is To get the post title and user display names of the posts that have positive comments, we can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT p.Title, u.UserDisplayName
FROM posts p
JOIN comments c ON p.Id = c.PostId
JOIN postHistory ph ON p.Id = ph.PostId
JOIN postLinks pl ON p.Id = pl.PostId
JOIN users u ON c.UserId = u.Id
WHERE c.Score > 60
```
This query joins the `posts`, `comments`, `postHistory`, `postLinks`, and `users` tables to get the posts that have a positive score (i.e., `c.Score > 60`). It then selects the `Title` of the post and the `UserDisplayName` of the user who made the positive comment.

The `JOIN` statements in this query use the foreign key relationships between the tables to link the data together. The `WHERE` clause filters the results to only include posts that have a positive score.

This query should return a list of post titles and user display names for the posts that have positive comments.
