flag is True, and result is Assuming that the table name is "postLinks" and the title of the post with the oldest post link should be the one associated with the oldest creation date among all the post links, the SQL query to get the title of the post with the oldest post link would be:
```vbnet
SELECT p.Title
FROM posts p
JOIN postLinks pl ON p.Id = pl.PostId
JOIN postHistory ph ON p.Id = ph.PostId
JOIN users u ON ph.UserId = u.Id
WHERE ph.CreationDate = (SELECT MIN(CreationDate) FROM postHistory);
```
The above query joins the "posts" table with the "postLinks" table on the "Id" column, and with the "postHistory" table on the "PostId" column. The "users" table is joined using the "UserId" column of the "postHistory" table to get the user who created the oldest post link. The WHERE clause filters the results to only include the post with the oldest creation date, which is the one with the oldest post link.

The query will return the title of the post with the oldest post link.
