flag is True, and result is To identify the number of posts and comments left by the user who has the latest created user account, we can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT COUNT(p.Id) as num_posts, COUNT(c.Id) as num_comments
FROM posts p
JOIN postHistory ph ON p.Id = ph.PostId
JOIN postLinks pl ON p.Id = pl.PostId
JOIN comments c ON c.Id = ph.CommentId
JOIN users u ON p.OwnerUserId = u.Id
WHERE u.CreationDate = (SELECT MAX(u2.CreationDate) FROM users u2)
GROUP BY u.Id
```
This query joins the `posts`, `postHistory`, `postLinks`, and `comments` tables and filters the results by the user with the latest created account (using the `WHERE` clause and the subquery in parentheses). The subquery in the `WHERE` clause finds the latest created user account by selecting the maximum `CreationDate` from the `users` table. The `SELECT COUNT()` function is then used to count the number of posts and comments left by that user. Finally, the results are grouped by the `Id` of the user using the `GROUP BY` clause.

This query will return the number of posts and comments left by the user with the latest created user account.
