flag is True, and result is To find the post ID and the comments commented in the post titled "Group differences on a five point Likert item," you can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT p.Id, c.Id
FROM posts p
JOIN comments c ON p.Id = c.PostId
WHERE p.Title = 'Group differences on a five point Likert item';
```
This query joins the `posts` and `comments` tables on the `PostId` foreign key, and selects the `Id` columns from both tables. It then filters the results by the title of the post, so only the post with the title "Group differences on a five point Likert item" is returned.

This query will return a table with two columns, `p.Id` and `c.Id`, which represent the post ID and the comment ID respectively. The comment ID is a foreign key that references the post ID in the `posts` table.
