flag is True, and result is To get the location coordinates of the circuits for the Australian Grand Prix from the 'circuits' table, you would need to join the 'circuits' table with itself to get the 'location' information for that circuit. Here's the SQL query you can use to get this information:
```sql
SELECT c1.name AS circuit_name, c1.lat AS latitude, c1.lng AS longitude, c2.name AS location
FROM circuits c1
JOIN circuits c2
ON c1.location = c2.name
WHERE c1.name = 'Australian Grand Prix';
```
This query selects the name of the circuit, its latitude, longitude, and the name of the location it is in. It joins the 'circuits' table with itself on the 'location' column, and filters the results to only include the 'Australian Grand Prix' circuit. The result set will contain one row with the name of the Australian Grand Prix circuit and its location coordinates.
