flag is True, and result is To find the season page of year when the race No. 901 took place, we need to join the races and seasons tables on the season\_id and year columns, respectively.

Here is the SQL query to achieve this:
```sql
SELECT s.year, s.url
FROM seasons s
JOIN races r ON r.year = s.year AND r.race_number = 901
```
Explanation:

* We start by selecting the year and url columns from the seasons table, which will give us the season page of year when the race No. 901 took place.
* We then join the seasons table with the races table on the season\_id and year columns, respectively.
* We also filter the races table by race\_number being equal to 901.

This query will return the year and url of the season page where race No. 901 took place.
