flag is True, and result is To answer the question "What time did the 2008's Formula\_1 race take place on the Albert Park Grand Prix Circuit?", we need to join the races and seasons tables on their respective foreign keys and then extract the start time of the race from the date field. We can use the following SQL query to achieve this:
```sql
SELECT start_time
FROM races
JOIN seasons ON races.year = seasons.year
WHERE races.name = '2008 Australian Grand Prix';
```
This query selects the start\_time field from the races table, and joins the seasons table on the races.year foreign key. The WHERE clause filters the results to only include the 2008 Australian Grand Prix race. The resulting start\_time value represents the time at which the race began, which should be the same as the start time of the race at Albert Park.
