flag is True, and result is To get the average time of rounds for each year, we need to first calculate the total time for each year and then divide it by the total number of rounds for that year. We can use the following query to get the required result:
```vbnet
SELECT year, AVG(SUM(time)/SUM(round)) as avg_time_round
FROM (
  SELECT 
    race.year, 
    race.round, 
    race.time, 
    COUNT(race.round) as round_count
  FROM races as race
  GROUP BY race.year, race.round, race.time
) as subquery
GROUP BY year;
```
In this query, we first select the year, round, and time from the races table and count the number of rounds for each year. We then group the results by year, round, and time and calculate the average time of rounds for each year using the AVG function.

