To achieve this, we can use a combination of the "select" and "where" clauses in a SQL query to filter the data based on the "year" column and the "name" column. Here is the SQL query to achieve this:
```sql
SELECT driverId, codeNumber, name
FROM drivers
WHERE year = (SELECT MIN(year) FROM drivers WHERE name LIKE '%Max%')
OR (SELECT MIN(year) FROM drivers WHERE name LIKE '%Brazil%')
ORDER BY year ASC
LIMIT 3;
```
