flag is True, and result is In the provided tables, we can answer this question by joining the races, drivers, and results tables and then grouping the results by race number. We can use the COUNT() function to count the number of finishers for each race number, and then find the race number with the highest count.

Here's the SQL query to answer the question:
```vbnet
SELECT races.year, races.name, races.round, races.date, races.time, races.url,
       COUNT(results.resultId) AS num_finishers,
       MAX(results.num_finishers) AS max_finishers
FROM races
JOIN drivers ON races.raceId = drivers.raceId
JOIN results ON races.raceId = results.raceId
GROUP BY races.year, races.name, races.round, races.date, races.time, races.url
ORDER BY max_finishers DESC;
```
This query will return the race number, year, name, round, date
