```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM drivers;
```
2. Find the maximum value of the nationality column in the drivers table:
```sql
SELECT MAX(nationality) FROM drivers;
```
3. Find the number of rows in the races table:
```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM races;
```
4. Find the maximum value of the nationality column in the races table:
```sql
SELECT MAX(nationality) FROM races;
```
5. Compare the result of step 2 with the result of step 4. If the majority of the drivers' nationality is different from the majority of the races' nationality, then the answer is "different". Otherwise, the answer is "the same".
```sql
IF (SELECT MAX(nationality) FROM drivers) <> (SELECT MAX(nationality) FROM races) THEN
    SELECT "Different";
ELSE
    SELECT "The same";
END
