flag is True, and result is SELECT name, MIN(fastestLapTime) AS fastestLapSpeed
FROM races
JOIN laptimes ON races.raceId = laptimes.raceId
GROUP BY races.raceId
ORDER BY fastestLapSpeed DESC
LIMIT 1;

This query will return the name of the race with the fastest lap speed recorded. It joins the races and laptimes tables on the raceId column, groups the results by raceId, and calculates the minimum fastestLapTime for each race. The results are then sorted in descending order by fastestLapSpeed and the top result is returned using the LIMIT 1 clause.
