flag is True, and result is To list all the football players with the highest potential score, we need to join the Player, Team, and League tables and use the MAX(potential) function to select the players with the highest potential score. The SQL query would be as follows:
```sql
SELECT p.name AS player_name, t.team_name, l.league_name, p.potential
FROM Player p
JOIN Team t ON p.team_api_id = t.team_api_id
JOIN League l ON t.league_id = l.league_id
WHERE p.potential = (SELECT MAX(potential) FROM Player);
```
This query will select the player name, team name, league name, and potential score from the Player, Team, and League tables, respectively. The WHERE clause filters the results to only include players with the highest potential score by using a subquery to find the maximum potential score in the Player table.
