flag is True, and result is To answer the question "What was the age of the youngest patient when they initially arrived at the hospital?", we need to use the "Patient" table and join it with the "Laboratory" table on the "ID" column. We also need to calculate the age of the patient by subtracting the year of their "First Date" from the year of their "Birthday".

Here is the SQL query to answer this question:
```
SELECT p.Birthday AS InitialArrivalAge, p.SEX, p.First Date, l.Date
FROM Patient p
JOIN Laboratory l ON p.ID = l.ID
WHERE p.SEX = 'Male' AND l.Date = (SELECT MIN(YEAR(birthday)) FROM Patient)
ORDER BY l.Date ASC
```
This query will return the "Birthday" (which is the year of the patient's birth), "SEX", "First Date", and "Date" (which is the date of their first laboratory test) of the youngest male patient, along with their age at the time of their initial arrival at the hospital (which is calculated as the year of their birth minus the year of their first laboratory test). The query will also sort the results by "Date" in ascending order.

