flag is True, and result is To answer this question, we can use the following steps:

1. Join the Patient and Laboratory tables on the ID and Date columns, respectively, to get the laboratory examination records for patient '48473'.
2. Filter the records to only include AST glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase (GOT) index values that are above the normal range (i.e., GOT > = 60).
3. Use the WHEN clause to only return the records that meet this condition.

Here is the SQL statement that implements these steps:
```
SELECT l.Date, p.ID, l.GOT
FROM Laboratory l
JOIN Patient p ON l.ID = p.ID AND l.Date = p.Birthday
WHERE l.GOT > 60 AND l.Date = (SELECT MAX(l2.Date) FROM Laboratory l2 WHERE l2.ID = l.ID AND l2.GOT > 60);
```
This query will return the date and patient ID of the laboratory examination for patient '48473' where the GOT index is above the normal range.
