flag is True, and result is Sure! Here is the SQL query to get the information you requested:
```vbnet
SELECT P.ID, P.Birthday, P.SEX, P.Diagnosis
FROM Patient P
JOIN Examination E ON P.ID = E.patient_id
JOIN Laboratory L ON E.lab_id = L.lab_id
WHERE L.ALB < 3.5 OR L.ALB > 5.5 AND P.SEX = 'M'
ORDER BY P.Birthday DESC;
```
This query will join the `Patient`, `Examination`, and `Laboratory` tables and filter the results to only include male patients with albumin levels outside of the normal range. It will then sort the results by birthday in descending order.

