flag is True, and result is To get the IDs of the patients with no thrombosis and an abnormal level of creatinine phosphokinase, we need to use a combination of the Laboratory and Patient tables.

First, we need to join the Laboratory table with the Patient table, and filter for patients who have no thrombosis (thrombosis = 0) and an abnormal level of creatinine phosphokinase (CPK < 250).
```sql
SELECT p.ID
FROM Patient p
JOIN Laboratory l ON p.ID = l.ID
WHERE l.Thrombosis = 0 AND l.CPK < 250;
```
This query will return the IDs of all patients who meet the criteria.

Next, we need to select the ID column from the Patient table, to get the names of the patients.
```sql
SELECT p.ID
FROM Patient p
JOIN Laboratory l ON p.ID = l.ID
WHERE l.Thrombosis = 0 AND l.CPK < 250;
```
This query will return the names of all patients who have no thrombosis and an abnormal level of creatinine phosphokinase.
