the question is: With the biggest budget for the "Food", what was the remaining of it?
models request {'model': 'vicuna-13b-1.1', 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'CREATE TABLE event\n(\n    event_id   TEXT\n        constraint event_pk\n            primary key,\n    event_name TEXT,\n    event_date TEXT,\n    type       TEXT,\n    notes      TEXT,\n    location   TEXT,\n    status     TEXT\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE major\n(\n    major_id   TEXT\n        constraint major_pk\n            primary key,\n    major_name TEXT,\n    department TEXT,\n    college    TEXT\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE zip_code\n(\n    zip_code    INTEGER\n        constraint zip_code_pk\n            primary key,\n    type        TEXT,\n    city        TEXT,\n    county      TEXT,\n    state       TEXT,\n    short_state TEXT\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "attendance"\n(\n    link_to_event  TEXT\n        constraint attendance_event_event_id_fk\n            references event,\n    link_to_member TEXT\n        constraint attendance_member_member_id_fk\n            references member,\n    constraint attendance_pk\n        primary key (link_to_event, link_to_member)\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "budget"\n(\n    budget_id     TEXT\n        constraint budget_pk\n            primary key,\n    category      TEXT,\n    spent         FLOAT,\n    remaining     FLOAT,\n    amount        INTEGER,\n    event_status  TEXT,\n    link_to_event TEXT\n        constraint budget_event_event_id_fk\n            references event\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "expense"\n(\n    expense_id          TEXT\n        constraint expense_pk\n            primary key,\n    expense_description TEXT,\n    expense_date        TEXT,\n    cost                REAL,\n    approved            TEXT,\n    link_to_member      TEXT\n        constraint expense_member_member_id_fk\n            references member,\n    link_to_budget      TEXT\n        constraint expense_budget_budget_id_fk\n            references budget\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "income"\n(\n    income_id      TEXT\n        constraint income_pk\n            primary key,\n    date_received  TEXT,\n    amount         INTEGER,\n    source         TEXT,\n    notes          TEXT,\n    link_to_member TEXT\n        constraint income_member_member_id_fk\n            references member\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "member"\n(\n    member_id     TEXT\n        constraint member_pk\n            primary key,\n    first_name    TEXT,\n    last_name     TEXT,\n    email         TEXT,\n    position      TEXT,\n    t_shirt_size  TEXT,\n    phone         TEXT,\n    zip           INTEGER\n        constraint member_zip_code_zip_code_fk\n            references zip_code,\n    link_to_major TEXT\n        references major\n)\n\n-- External Knowledge: remaining of budget refers to remaining, biggest budget for \'Food\' refers to MAX(budget.amount) where category = \'Food\'\n-- Using valid SQLite and understading External Knowledge, answer the following questions for the tables provided above.\n-- With the biggest budget for the "Food", what was the remaining of it?\nGenerate the SQL after thinking step by step: \nSELECT '}]}
flag is True, and result is SELECT MAX(b.amount) as max\_budget\_amount, b.remaining
FROM budget b
JOIN expense e ON b.event\_status = e.event\_status
JOIN income i ON e.link\_to\_member = i.link\_to\_member
WHERE b.category = 'Food'
GROUP BY b.event\_id;

This query will first join the budget, expense, and income tables on their respective foreign keys (event\_id, event\_id, and link\_to\_event/budget\_id), and then group the results by the event\_id. The MAX() function is used to find the budget with the highest amount for the category 'Food'. The WHERE clause filters the results to only include budgets with a category of 'Food'. Finally, the GROUP BY clause groups the results by event\_id, which is also the primary key of the budget table. The result of this query will be a table with two columns: max\_budget\_amount and remaining, which represent the maximum budget amount and the remaining budget amount for the event with the highest budget amount in the 'Food' category, respectively.
