models request {'model': 'vicuna-13b-1.1', 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'CREATE TABLE event\n(\n    event_id   TEXT\n        constraint event_pk\n            primary key,\n    event_name TEXT,\n    event_date TEXT,\n    type       TEXT,\n    notes      TEXT,\n    location   TEXT,\n    status     TEXT\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE major\n(\n    major_id   TEXT\n        constraint major_pk\n            primary key,\n    major_name TEXT,\n    department TEXT,\n    college    TEXT\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE zip_code\n(\n    zip_code    INTEGER\n        constraint zip_code_pk\n            primary key,\n    type        TEXT,\n    city        TEXT,\n    county      TEXT,\n    state       TEXT,\n    short_state TEXT\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "attendance"\n(\n    link_to_event  TEXT\n        constraint attendance_event_event_id_fk\n            references event,\n    link_to_member TEXT\n        constraint attendance_member_member_id_fk\n            references member,\n    constraint attendance_pk\n        primary key (link_to_event, link_to_member)\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "budget"\n(\n    budget_id     TEXT\n        constraint budget_pk\n            primary key,\n    category      TEXT,\n    spent         FLOAT,\n    remaining     FLOAT,\n    amount        INTEGER,\n    event_status  TEXT,\n    link_to_event TEXT\n        constraint budget_event_event_id_fk\n            references event\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "expense"\n(\n    expense_id          TEXT\n        constraint expense_pk\n            primary key,\n    expense_description TEXT,\n    expense_date        TEXT,\n    cost                REAL,\n    approved            TEXT,\n    link_to_member      TEXT\n        constraint expense_member_member_id_fk\n            references member,\n    link_to_budget      TEXT\n        constraint expense_budget_budget_id_fk\n            references budget\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "income"\n(\n    income_id      TEXT\n        constraint income_pk\n            primary key,\n    date_received  TEXT,\n    amount         INTEGER,\n    source         TEXT,\n    notes          TEXT,\n    link_to_member TEXT\n        constraint income_member_member_id_fk\n            references member\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "member"\n(\n    member_id     TEXT\n        constraint member_pk\n            primary key,\n    first_name    TEXT,\n    last_name     TEXT,\n    email         TEXT,\n    position      TEXT,\n    t_shirt_size  TEXT,\n    phone         TEXT,\n    zip           INTEGER\n        constraint member_zip_code_zip_code_fk\n            references zip_code,\n    link_to_major TEXT\n        references major\n)\n\n-- External Knowledge: major in refers to major_name\n-- Using valid SQLite and understading External Knowledge, answer the following questions for the tables provided above.\n-- What does the person with the phone number "809-555-3360" major in?\nGenerate the SQL after thinking step by step: \nSELECT '}]}
flag is True, and result is major.major\_name
FROM "member"
JOIN "attendance" ON member.member\_id = attendance.link\_to\_member
JOIN "budget" ON attendance.link\_to\_event = budget.link\_to\_event
JOIN "zip\_code" ON budget.zip\_code = zip\_code.zip\_code
JOIN "major" ON member.link\_to\_major = major.major\_name
WHERE "attendance"."link\_to\_event" = '809-555-3360'
;

This query will retrieve the name of the major of the person whose phone number is '809-555-3360' by joining the 'member', 'attendance', 'budget', 'zip\_code', and 'major' table. It will first join the 'attendance' table on the 'link\_to\_member' column and the 'budget' table on the 'link\_to\_event' column. Then it will join the 'zip\_code' table on the 'zip\_code' column and the 'major' table on the 'major\_name' column. Finally, it will filter the result by the phone number '809-555-3360' so that only the relevant row from the 'attendance' table is selected, and the query will return the major\_name of the person whose phone number is '809-555-3360'.
