  INTEGER,\n    source         TEXT,\n    notes          TEXT,\n    link_to_member TEXT\n        constraint income_member_member_id_fk\n            references member\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "member"\n(\n    member_id     TEXT\n        constraint member_pk\n            primary key,\n    first_name    TEXT,\n    last_name     TEXT,\n    email         TEXT,\n    position      TEXT,\n    t_shirt_size  TEXT,\n    phone         TEXT,\n    zip           INTEGER\n        constraint member_zip_code_zip_code_fk\n            references zip_code,\n    link_to_major TEXT\n        references major\n)\n\n-- External Knowledge: expense refers to expense_description; \'Vice President\' is a position of the Student Club\n-- Using valid SQLite and understading External Knowledge, answer the following questions for the tables provided above.\n-- List all the expenses incurred by the vice president.\nGenerate the SQL after thinking step by step: \nSELECT '}]}
flag is True, and result is 1. First, we need to create a foreign key constraint that references the "member" table, so we can link the expenses to the vice president:
```sql
ALTER TABLE expense ADD FOREIGN KEY (link_to_member) REFERENCES member(member_id);
```
2. Then, we can use the following SQL statement to retrieve all the expenses incurred by the vice president:
```sql
SELECT * FROM expense
WHERE link_to_member = (SELECT member_id FROM member WHERE position = 'Vice President');
```
This query will select all the rows from the "expense" table where the "link\_to\_member" column is equal to the member\_id of the vice president.

3. To get the expense description, cost, and date of the expense, we can use the following SQL statement:
```sql
SELECT expense_description, cost, expense_date FROM expense
WHERE link_to_member = (SELECT member_id FROM member WHERE position = 'Vice President');
```
This query will select the "expense\_description", "cost", and "expense\_date" columns from the "expense" table, but only for the rows where the "link\_to\_member" column is equal to the member\_id of the vice president.
