  INTEGER,\n    source         TEXT,\n    notes          TEXT,\n    link_to_member TEXT\n        constraint income_member_member_id_fk\n            references member\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE "member"\n(\n    member_id     TEXT\n        constraint member_pk\n            primary key,\n    first_name    TEXT,\n    last_name     TEXT,\n    email         TEXT,\n    position      TEXT,\n    t_shirt_size  TEXT,\n    phone         TEXT,\n    zip           INTEGER\n        constraint member_zip_code_zip_code_fk\n            references zip_code,\n    link_to_major TEXT\n        references major\n)\n\n-- External Knowledge: zip codes that have post office boxes refers to type = \'PO Box\'\n-- Using valid SQLite and understading External Knowledge, answer the following questions for the tables provided above.\n-- Which countries have zip codes with post office boxes?\nGenerate the SQL after thinking step by step: \nSELECT '}]}
flag is True, and result is SELECT m.first\_name, m.last\_name
FROM "member" m
JOIN "attendance" a ON m.link\_to\_member = a.link\_to\_member
JOIN "budget" b ON a.link\_to\_event = b.link\_to\_event
JOIN "expense" e ON b.link\_to\_budget = e.link\_to\_budget
WHERE e.cost > 100 AND e.approved = 'yes' AND b.event\_status = 'approved'
ORDER BY m.last\_name;

This query will select the first and last name of all members that have attended an approved event with a cost greater than 100 dollars and have an expense approved with a budget that has an event status of approved. The query will order the results by last name.
